[Music]  the vegan diet has been gaining  popularity in recent years and today i  want to share with you my experience  with veganism and share why i'm no  longer vegan i'm first going to begin by  talking about why i became vegan in the  first place and then i'll share with you  my three main reasons for why i'm no  longer vegan the first two are really  just main food categories that i had  issues with when it came to veganism and  then my third reason is really where i  talk about the health issues that i  faced and what i decided to do about it  also please note that the information is  time stamped below so you can skip to  your heart's content and if you like  this video please give it a thumbs up to  help support my channel and if not by  all means thumbs it down but please give  me some feedback in the comments so that  i know what to work on and i have to  include this disclaimer i am not a  doctor i'm not trying to tell you what  to do as far as your diet i'm really  only sharing my experience in the hopes  that it's helpful for you and  encouraging for you so please consult  with your doctor before you make any  changes to your diet i started a vegan  diet about five to six years ago after  binge watching the documentaries food  inc forks over knives and what the hell  after watching these documentaries my  eyes were open to the tremendous changes  in the food industry throughout the last  few decades our food is not what it used  to be with added hormones and chemicals  and gmos and most of the foods now on  the market after watching these  documentaries i never could see a piece  of bacon the same in a grocery store i  couldn't i found myself standing in the  deli section and remembering that farmer  talking about his struggle or the impact  of those big processing plans on the  environment the abuse that the workers  face  it suddenly felt personal it felt like  not only was it impacting my health but  it was impacting the life of my  community  so after watching these films it was  like this fire was lit inside of me and  i was wanting everybody to watch them  and i was out buying these cds and  copies so that i could send them to my  friends and family and i tossed all the  junk food all the meats and the dairy  and i started with a blank slate  or a blank pantry and let me just tell  you that as a mexican when you tell  people that you're not gonna eat  carnitas or carne asada people look at  you like  but that wasn't really a problem for me  i sincerely believe that the reason that  people judged me was because they didn't  know the impact that their eating  choices were having on their health and  the environment my first issue with  veganism began with these little cows  eggs  you see my husband and i both grew up on  farms so when i told him that i wanted  to have chickens he was all for it  actually the conversation kind of went  more like this if you want to marry me  we're going to have chickens in the yard  in all of the research that i found  about eggs i mainly found information  about their high cholesterol content or  the types of feed that the chickens are  given but i figured if the high content  of cholesterol is really in the egg yolk  and our chickens are running around  eating grass and bugs  then why not just eat egg whites  i never really liked egg yolks anyway so  it made sense to me to reduce the  quantity of egg yolks but i didn't  really find any data to support  eliminating eggs from our diet  altogether because i have these fat  fluffy things giving me free eggs every  day and i'm gonna let their kind gifts  go to waste  i think not  the next reason for why i'm not vegan is  this delicious delicacy  some vegans omit honey from their diet  to avoid or minimize all forms of animal  exploitation  and i have a big problem with this and  let me tell you why you hear a lot of  talk about saving the polar bears or  saving the animals from near extinction  but at least for me i had never heard  that honeybees are in danger with an  ever-increasing use of pesticides the  bee population is decreasing at a rapid  rate and this should scare us this  should definitely be something that  we're talking about and sharing but  there's definitely a lack of awareness  on this issue if we think back to our  school days you may remember that bees  are an important part of the pollination  process which helps our gardens to  flourish so for this reason i'm very  adamant about not only avoiding the use  of pesticides in our garden but also  supporting our local bee farmers with  big corporations making processed honey  much cheaper than the bee farmers can  sell for a lot of bee farmers have gone  out of business and this to me is a huge  loss not only for the bee farmers but  for our communities because not only are  we killing our bees with pesticides but  we're also choosing to support the  companies that make the cheap process  deluded jug over supporting the farmers  that are actually helping to increase  the bee population and better our  environment so this to me is like a  double whammy  i look at it this way the cheap brands  may be better for my wallet but i choose  the more expensive price tag as my way  of supporting local bee farmers so that  they can continue helping the  environment and increasing the bee  population because i for sure don't see  myself ever being a bee farmer  also as a fun side note honey never  expires so you can stockpile it for that  zombie apocalypse  and my third and most important reason  for why i'm not vegan is it is not a  diet that is healthy for everyone  those of you who have seen my previous  videos may be aware that i had recently  given birth and i touched on the fact  that i had some health issues during the  pregnancy  i had some symptoms that were just off i  had anxiety for no reason at all with  heart palpitations and this feeling like  a bear was chasing me like i had to  catch my breath for no reason at all  like even just lying in bed doing  nothing super dry skin joint pain other  symptoms let me not bore you with the  list  but it just felt like it wasn't just  pregnancy i had been pregnant before so  i knew that some of these things were  normal like fatigue but something in my  gut just said there's something else  after seeing several doctors and having  several blood tests i was finally  diagnosed with hashimoto's thyroiditis  and i was found to be hyperthyroid  during my pregnancy especially i had to  be checked very frequently because  pregnant women with this condition are  much more likely to have a miscarriage  and babies born to mothers with this  condition  are also more likely to have birth  defects  so this kept me at doctor's offices a  lot during pregnancy and postpartum so  after i learned that i had this i tried  to learn everything that i could about  it what causes it what makes it worse  what makes it better is there a cure i  had hundreds of questions i still have  questions  in my research on hashimoto's i stumbled  upon dr weston's youtube channel where  he talks about the link between  hashimoto's and diet  and i couldn't help but ask myself  but how i eat a plant-based diet i eat  veggies every day i rarely eat fried  foods i don't drink sodas and for the  most part if i want a pastry i make  myself with replacements for oil and  flour like my delicious pumpkin brownies  you see i genuinely believed that a  vegan plant-based diet could cure almost  everything and so i was shocked to find  out that i was hyperthyroid and not only  that but my rheumatologist also found  out that i was low in vitamin b12 and  vitamin d  and my diagnosis changed my perspective  of food even further  because before i had a very black and  white way of seeing food foods were  either in one of two categories good or  bad  tomatoes good  cake bad  but the more i researched the  hashimoto's diet the more confused i got  some of the dietary restrictions that  are recommended didn't really surprise  me like caffeine wheat gluten sugars  artificial sweeteners but you see  apparently some of the things that we  consider as good and healthy for most  people  are actually harmful for people with  this condition this includes things like  nightshades like tomatoes and tomatillos  eggplants potatoes peppers rice and corn  even peanut butter and some nuts can  also be inflammatory  this all baffled me because these were  all foods that i consider to be good  they can't cause my body harm they're  vegan  but then it got even stickier because  i'm trying to make a list of what i can  eat and what i can't  and then i'm finding conflicting  information certain sources would say  that these things are good and okay and  certain sources would say that these  things are not things like soy eggs  mushrooms and oatmeal so i found myself  very confused and thinking  what am i supposed to eat  celery sticks in water  my reaction quickly changed from that of  empowerment to overwhelm and anxiety  because the list of foods to avoid is  quite extensive and for someone who's  already on somewhat of a restricted diet  to all of a sudden learn all sorts of  new restrictions to take this was very  disappointing and honestly it led me to  unhealthy thoughts for a few weeks all i  could think about all day long was food  i would wake up and think what can i eat  or the day would go by and i would think  what can i cook that i can eat but my  own family can also enjoy or my husband  and i would go out to eat and i would  feel guilty for having had a sandwich  because i know i shouldn't have bread  where my family would make comments such  as aren't you not supposed to eat that  it got to a point where i would  literally wake up every night or every  morning with dreams about food and my  nightmares or that i was eating a slice  of chocolate cake  because i love me some chocolate cake  you guys  and i'm ashamed to admit that it felt  like i was going to spiral into anorexic  tendencies pretty quickly if i didn't  reset this behavior because it felt like  i had no control guilt was a constant  part of my day and i felt like i had to  hide food or eat it quickly before  someone noticed or made a comment and  food was all i could think about all day  long it became an obsession  and i began to feel like if what i'm  going to be eating or not eating is  going to be governed by others judged by  others or i'm going to be feeling guilty  for it then i just won't eat simple  problem solved but would that really  solve my problems will that really  restore my health would that really  truly bring me peace and happiness the  answer was of course no to all of these  so besides prayer i did what i usually  do when i'm not sure why i'm having  negative thoughts or what to do about  them i journaled  i poured it all out and i sifted through  the mess to try to figure out how i  could restore balance and for me the  conclusion was this i'm trying my best  to eat the diet that is best for me but  i'm finding conflicting information and  it feels like i'm stuck in a game of  ping pong and i'm the ball and i don't  want to live with constant feelings of  shame and guilt because of what i am or  am not eating i genuinely want to  nurture my body and live a healthy and  fulfilling life while also reducing my  carbon footprint but the very thing that  was supposed to help me and nurture me  food had become my obsession so i  decided i was done i don't want any part  of that i don't want to have to hide if  i eat something that i know i shouldn't  have or if i do eat it i don't want to  feel shame for what i did i want to  actually enjoy it and make it worth it i  think the biggest realization for me has  been this i have to have balance i do  still choose to have a mostly  anti-inflammatory diet i avoid dairy and  most meats but i don't beat myself up if  i want a slice of chocolate cake for my  birthday and if you were to invite me to  your cookout and all you had was  barbecue sandwiches even though i really  don't like barbecue i would still eat it  out of respect for you and gratitude for  your kindness at the end of the day i  still believe that a healthy diet is  crucial for good health but i no longer  believe that there's one diet that is  perfect for everyone our daughter has  also had her own health journey as she's  in the long process of being evaluated  for autism and the more i research about  that the more i learn that she has her  own sensitivities and her own  recommendations for things that she  should avoid that are specific to her  different than they are to me so there's  that part there's the aspect that not  one diet doesn't fit all but also i  believe that our thoughts are powerful  and the thoughts and feelings that i was  having towards food were typical of  individuals with eating disorders  and i haven't shared this with you guys  but i've actually been down that road  before i once dropped to 98 pounds at  five foot seven in a period of  depression after experiencing a loss and  i don't want that for myself i want to  be the best me that i can be and be  healthy enjoy life to the fullest and  give my best  so the diet that is best for me  is balance  i will continue to eat a plant-based  diet but if i have a slice of pizza at a  birthday party that's okay i'm okay with  that  my hope for you is that if you have  feelings of frustration shame guilt  obsession and respect to food that you  focus on doing the best that you can do  and don't beat yourself up if you make  one unhealthy choice  and always offer the diet that is  healthy and right for you just because a  diet works for somebody else doesn't  mean that it will work for you or be  healthy for you  if you've made it to the end my hope is  that you make the choice today to learn  about how your eating choices impact  your health but also the world as a  whole the documentaries that i mentioned  in the beginning have still been  life-changing for me  and some of them are  gut-wrenching and eye-opening i couldn't  help but just want to jump in the screen  and help those individuals but you know  what we can help it begins with us it  begins with you it begins with me so  let's make the choice today to better  our health but also the health of our  environment and let me know have you  ever tried a vegan diet what is your  current diet and what are your thoughts  i'd love to hear from you i thank you so  much for watching until next time bye  [Music]

